/sundown_mark_moon_afe9ec5da6/public",{"public_id":1693,"resource_type":1697},"optimized-sundown_mark_moon_afe9ec5da6","2026-03-06T20:19:55.931Z",{"data":1700},{"id":6,"attributes":1701},{"name":1479,"createdAt":1480,"updatedAt":1481,"publishedAt":1482},{"id":1703,"spotify":8,"apple":1704,"deezer":8,"youtube":8,"mixcloud":8,"amazon":8,"soundcloud":8},121,"https://music.apple.com/gb/album/cafe-del-mar-sundown-mix-vol-5-dj-mix/1878429612",{"data":1706},{"id":1707,"attributes":1708},31,{"name":1538,"bio":1709,"pressPhotos":8,"createdAt":1710,"updatedAt":1711,"publishedAt":1712,"slug":1713,"image":1714,"socials":1751},"Mark Lobensteijn has been a producer since the late 1980s. \nBorn and raised in the Hague region of the Netherlands in 1969, he \ngrew up surrounded by many different kinds of music, ranging from \njazz, bossa nova, classical and folk to early electronic pioneers such \nas Kraftwerk, Tangerine Dream, Tomita, Giorgio Moroder and Gino Soccio. \n\nIn 2025 he released a new Mark Moon album titled “Music for the Illusive Mind”, a downtempo and Balearic influenced project featuring ten tracks and running just over an hour. The album further explores his signature blend of atmospheric electronics, ambient grooves and melodic storytelling. \nThe project also led to renewed collaboration with the legendary Café del Mar Music label, known worldwide for its iconic chill-out compilations and sunset sound. Just recently this resulted in the release of the “” on Café del Mar Music, featuring several tracks including “Maison Du Jouir”, as well as the original versions of “Jill” by Mark’s & Henry’s and “Abo Road” by Global Dance Project, bringing two early highlights from Mark’s catalogue back into the Café del Mar universe. ","2026-03-06T20:21:48.393Z","2026-07-27T00:57:33.387Z","2026-03-06T20:21:49.865Z","mark-moon",{"data":1715},{"id":1716,"attributes":1717},345,{"name":1718,"alternativeText":8,"caption":8,"width":1719,"height":1719,"formats":1720,"hash":1745,"ext":17